SOAPBOX: Wow! This is something completely new in contesting! I see a lot of
SOAPBOX: potential for the World Wide Digi DX Contest to lead development of the
SOAPBOX: future of contesting. With the fast pace of development in digital modes
SOAPBOX: and the rise of live scoring, radiosport has the potential to be
SOAPBOX: attractive as an e-sport to young hams. This can certainly help
SOAPBOX: revitalise ham radio!
SOAPBOX: I could only be on sporadically this weekend due to social engagements.
SOAPBOX: During setup before the contest I had challenges with WSJT-X controlling
SOAPBOX: the rig through N1MM+. Lack of time forced me to do a quick and dirty
SOAPBOX: fix, ie. control CAT from WSJT-X instead. I also had some issues with
SOAPBOX: call checking in N1MM making all calls appear as not worked. With the
SOAPBOX: little operating time I had planned I didn't bother, I wasn't aiming to
SOAPBOX: score big anyway.
SOAPBOX: 85 contacts where logged at a slow rate, it was hard to get real runs
SOAPBOX: going so I worked a combination of Run and S&P. My focus was on FT4 and
SOAPBOX: even at high power it was a struggle to complete contacts with the lousy
SOAPBOX: propagation. Quite a few responded to my CQ calls, but after given the
SOAPBOX: exchange they disappeared. Maybe the QRM levels and propagation didn't
SOAPBOX: provide the signal path needed for completing the contacts. The final
SOAPBOX: score was microscopic 2120 points.
SOAPBOX: There is also an update on my blog, www.se0x.info.
SOAPBOX: 73!
